# Epidemiological Time-Series Trend Forecasting & Visual Analytics

An end-to-end epidemiological time-series analysis and forecasting pipeline built in Python using **Pandas**, **Facebook Prophet**, **Plotly**, and **Matplotlib** to track regional COVID-19 case trajectories, compute daily incidence rates and rolling averages, and generate 7-day forward projections with confidence intervals[cite: 14].

## Analytical Pipeline Flow

```text
Raw Daily Case Datasets (CSV / Excel: Confirmed, Recovered, Deaths)
        │
        ▼
Data Wrangling & Datetime Standardization (pd.to_datetime & Regional Aggregation)
        │
        ├──▶ Time-Series Feature Engineering
        │       ├── Active Cases Calculation (Confirmed - Recovered - Deaths)
        │       ├── Daily Incidence Rate (.diff())
        │       └── 7-Day Rolling Moving Average (.rolling(7).mean())
        │
        ▼
Facebook Prophet Time-Series Forecasting (ds, y Schema)
        │
        ▼
7-Day Forward Projections (yhat, yhat_lower, yhat_upper) & Interactive Visuals (Plotly / Matplotlib)
```

## Key Technical Highlights
- **Multi-Source Time-Series Wrangling:** Consolidated daily confirmed, recovered, and mortality records into standardized date-indexed time-series tables across regional cohorts[cite: 14].
- **Incidence & Trend Smoothing:** Engineered daily new-case velocity metrics using `.diff()` alongside 7-day rolling averages to filter reporting noise and highlight inflection points[cite: 14].
- **Prophet Forecasting & Uncertainty Intervals:** Formatted historical trajectories into Prophet's `ds` (datestamp) and `y` (target metric) schema to generate 7-day forward forecasts with upper and lower confidence bounds (`yhat_lower`, `yhat_upper`)[cite: 14].
- **Interactive & Static Visual Analytics:** Built interactive trajectory plots in **Plotly** and component/trend diagnostic charts in **Matplotlib**[cite: 14].

## Tech Stack
- **Data Manipulation & Time-Series Processing:** Python, Pandas, NumPy[cite: 14]
- **Forecasting Engine:** Facebook Prophet (`prophet`)[cite: 14]
- **Data Visualization:** Plotly, Matplotlib[cite: 14]

## Setup & Execution
1. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```
2. Open the Jupyter Notebook in JupyterLab or Google Colab and run all cells to reproduce the incidence calculations, interactive charts, and 7-day Prophet forecast plots[cite: 14].
